PHYTEC Yocto Linux BSP: phy²octo
===============================
Download the phyLinux tool from phytec to your yocto build folder

$: ./phyLinux

or you can use repo manually

To get the BSP you need to have `repo` installed and use it as:

Install the `repo` utility:

$: mkdir ~/bin
$: curl http://commondatastorage.googleapis.com/git-repo-downloads/repo > ~/bin/repo
$: chmod a+x ~/bin/repo
$: PATH=${PATH}:~/bin

Download the BSP source:

$: mkdir yocto
$: cd yocto
$: repo init -u git://git.phytec.de/phy2octo -b <soc> -m <release>
$: repo sync


Yocto Common Tasks
===============================
Put these lines in you local.conf to make it work just for your
local build. For permanently applying the options you have to put it
at the systematically correct spot in your yocto build.

# install the kernel modules to rootfs
IMAGE_INSTALL += "kernel-modules"

# install barebox tools into rootfs
IMAGE_INSTALL += "barebox-dev"

# install something in the initramfs
PACKAGE_INSTALL_append

# build sd card image
IMAGE_FSTYPES += "sdimg-phy"

# build commercial software packages
LICENSE_FLAGS_WHITELIST = "commercial"

# add touchscreen to machine
MACHINE_FEATURES += "touchscreen"

#global sources mirror before premirror
# only one url possible
INHERIT += "own-mirrors"
SOURCE_MIRROR_URL = "ftp://ftp.phytec.de/pub/BSP_PACKAGES/yoctomirror"

# use CCACHE
CCACHE = "ccache"
INHERIT += "ccache"
CCACHE_DIR = "<home>/.ccache"
CCACHE_DISABLE = "0"

# uboot variables to configure
UBOOT_ARCH = "arm"
UBOOT_MACHINE = "am335x_evm_config"
UBOOT_ENTRYPOINT = "0x80008000"
UBOOT_LOADADDRESS = "0x80008000"

#open gl TI
MACHINE_FEATURES += "sgx"



# Custom Barebox environment
# place it in the following folder
# <yocto>/meta-phytec/meta-phy<soc>/recipes-bsp/barebox/env/<machine>/environment

